// .workflow/DW-2-issue.md with contact details and hosts replaced, for parser tests.
// Regenerate with the script in tests/fixtures/README.md.
export default "# Issue: Agent Plugins compatibility for non-Claude agents\n\n**Source**: manual description (`tasks/DW-2_agent-plugins-compatibility.md`)\n**Source type**: manual\n**Parent**: none\n**Additional context**: `tasks/DW-2_agent-plugins-compatibility.md`, Agent Plugins spec 1.0.0/1.1.0, Agent Skills spec, Claude Code plugins reference, local `~/.cursor` and `~/.agents` skill installs\n**Date**: 2026-08-21\n**Branch**: feature/DW-2_agent-plugins-compatibility\n**Base branch**: main\n**Status**: Clarified \u2014 awaiting planning\n\n## Problem Statement\n\nThis plugin is packaged for Claude Code alone. A vendor-neutral packaging standard now exists \u2014\n**Agent Plugins 1.0.0**, published 2026-08-06 and supported by ChatGPT, Codex, Cursor, GitHub\nCopilot, Kiro, and VS Code \u2014 and this plugin is one file away from conforming to it.\n\nThe skills themselves already fit: `skills/<name>/SKILL.md` *is* the Agent Plugins layout, every\nskill's `name` matches its directory, and every description is far under the 1024-character cap.\nThe only structural blocker is the manifest. The spec requires `plugin.json` at the **plugin\nroot**; Claude Code reads `.claude-plugin/plugin.json`. Two different paths, so two files must\ncoexist \u2014 and the current manifest could not serve as the portable one anyway, because the\nportable schema is closed and our manifest carries two fields it forbids (`displayName`,\n`skills`) while missing the required `$schema`.\n\nThe task is to add the portable manifest without disturbing anything Claude Code relies on.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nA new root `plugin.json`, valid against the published 1.0.0 schema, sitting alongside an\n**untouched** `.claude-plugin/plugin.json`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://agent-plugins.org/schemas/1.0.0/plugin.schema.json\",\n  \"name\": \"dev-workflow\",\n  \"version\": \"1.7.1\",\n  \"description\": \"Structured, multi-step development workflow: clarify \u2192 plan \u2192 \u2026\",\n  \"author\": { \"name\": \"Aleksandr Mitasov\", \"email\": \"author@example.com\" },\n  \"license\": \"MIT\",\n  \"keywords\": [\"workflow\", \"tdd\", \"planning\", \"code-review\", \"release\"],\n  \"repository\": \"https://git.example.com/ai-tools/dev-workflow\"\n}\n```\n\nThe change is **purely additive** \u2014 one new file. No `SKILL.md` is edited, and no field is\nremoved from the Claude manifest.\n\n## Design Decisions\n\nSettled during clarification; inputs to planning, not open questions.\n\n1. **Manifest only.** No `SKILL.md` is touched in this task.\n2. **Keep both manifests, unchanged.** `displayName` and `skills` are *recognized Claude Code\n   fields* \u2014 illegal only in the portable schema, which does not govern `.claude-plugin/`.\n   Removing them would delete working config, not tidy it. Verified: `claude plugin validate .\n   --strict` reports no field warnings today.\n3. **Duplicate the `version` in both manifests**, and record the drift risk as a\n   `CLAUDE.local.md` gotcha. `version` is optional in the portable schema and omitting it would\n   have removed the risk outright, but a versionless plugin in non-Claude clients was judged the\n   worse trade. Mitigation is a note, matching how the triplicated commit-detection block is\n   already handled.\n4. **`repository` is set** to `https://git.example.com/ai-tools/dev-workflow` \u2014 the\n   conventional GitLab web URL derived from the SSH remote. Not reachable from the dev machine\n   to confirm.\n5. **Root manifest only.** No `.codex-plugin/` or `.cursor-plugin/` manifests; rely on those\n   clients honouring the spec they co-authored. Revisit only if one demonstrably fails to load.\n6. **Frontmatter is left alone** \u2014 see Edge Cases.\n7. **Target 1.0.0, not 1.1.0.** 1.0.0 is published; 1.1.0 is a Working Draft. Their plugin\n   schemas were verified to have an identical field set, so 1.0.0 is forward-compatible.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Given the repo root, When the plugin is inspected, Then `plugin.json` exists and validates against the Agent Plugins 1.0.0 schema\n- [ ] Given `.claude-plugin/plugin.json`, When compared to its pre-change state, Then it is byte-identical apart from any version bump\n- [ ] Given `claude plugin validate . --strict`, Then it reports no *new* warnings beyond the pre-existing `CLAUDE.local.md at plugin root` one\n- [ ] Given both manifests, Then `version` is identical in each\n- [ ] Given all 18 skills, When they are listed, Then no `SKILL.md` has been modified\n- [ ] Given `CLAUDE.local.md`, Then a gotcha records that the version now lives in two manifests and bumping one alone is silent\n- [ ] Given `README.md`, Then it states Agent Plugins 1.0.0 conformance and explains the dual-manifest arrangement\n- [ ] Given `README.md`, Then the skill count reads 18, not 17\n\n## Affected Components\n\n- `plugin.json` \u2014 **new**, at repo root; the portable manifest and the whole point of the task\n- `.claude-plugin/plugin.json` \u2014 deliberately unchanged; named here so a reviewer knows that is intentional, not an oversight\n- `CLAUDE.local.md` \u2014 new gotcha for the duplicated version\n- `README.md` \u2014 compatibility section; also carries a stale skill count (says 17, there are 18)\n- `.claude-plugin/plugin.json` **version bump** \u2014 this task ships as a release, so the version moves in both manifests together\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Scenarios\n\n- **Version drift between the two manifests.** Accepted under decision 3 and mitigated only by a\n  note. Sharpened during clarification: **`/workflow-release` does not bump any version file** \u2014\n  it computes the SemVer bump, writes `CHANGELOG.md`, commits, and tags, but every historical\n  bump (`1.6.0`, `1.7.0`, `1.7.1`) was made by hand during *implementation*. So the mitigation\n  rests on whoever implements remembering, with no skill step enforcing it.\n- **Frontmatter is non-conformant and stays that way.** All 18 skills fail the official\n  reference validator on `argument-hint`, `model`, and `disable-model-invocation`:\n  `skills-ref validate skills/workflow-release` \u2192\n  *\"Unexpected fields in frontmatter \u2026 Only \\['allowed-tools','compatibility','description','license','metadata','name'\\] are allowed.\"*\n  Agent Plugins \u00a77.1 says a client MUST *skip* a non-conformant skill. In practice clients do\n  not: Cursor's own first-party skills (`goal`, `rename-chat`, `migrate-to-skills` in\n  `~/.cursor/skills-cursor/`) use `disable-model-invocation` themselves and add further non-spec\n  fields (`environments`, `disabled-environments`), and Claude Code documents that it ignores\n  unrecognized fields. Stripping the field would let an agent autonomously run\n  `/workflow-release`, `/workflow-commit`, or `/workflow-commit-dev` \u2014 skills that commit, tag,\n  and push. **The guarantee is worth more than the validator.**\n- **That leniency is observed, not promised.** A future strict client would skip all 18 skills.\n  Re-test if a target client starts enforcing \u00a77.1.\n- **`$schema` pins a spec version.** Moving to 1.1.0 later means editing the URL \u2014 a second\n  version string in the same file, independent of `version`.\n- **`repository` URL is unverified** from this machine and may 404.\n- **A root `plugin.json` is a new file in Claude Code's plugin root.** Claude Code ignores\n  unrecognized root files, so this is expected to be inert \u2014 but it is untested here.\n\n## Dependencies & Blockers\n\n- None external. One new JSON file plus two documentation edits.\n- No build, test, or lint tooling in this repo \u2014 but `claude plugin validate . --strict` exists\n  and should serve as the verification step.\n- **Not verified**: Codex CLI is not installed on this machine, so Codex-side loading is\n  unproven. Cursor was never exercised end-to-end either; the evidence is its shipped skill\n  files, not an observed load of this plugin.\n\n## Open Questions\n\n- (none \u2014 all three resolved during clarification: version duplicated with a gotcha,\n  `repository` set to the HTTPS GitLab URL, root manifest only)\n\n## Implementation Plan\n\n**Mode**: Regular\n**Complexity**: Low\n**Steps**: 5\n\nFull plan file: `~/.claude/plans/purrfect-yawning-cat.md`\n\nTwo scope additions were settled during planning: the version bump is **minor \u2192 1.8.0**, and\nthe undocumented `/workflow-jira-report` gets a README bullet (found while correcting the stale\nskill counts \u2014 a corrected count of 18 that still listed 17 skills would read as a new error).\n\n### Step 1: Bump the version in `.claude-plugin/plugin.json`\n- **Action**: `1.7.1` \u2192 `1.8.0`. Minor: new capability, fully backward compatible.\n- **Files**: `.claude-plugin/plugin.json` \u2014 modify\n- **Verify**: `grep '\"version\"' .claude-plugin/plugin.json` \u2192 `1.8.0`\n\n### Step 2: Create the portable root manifest\n- **Action**: New `plugin.json` at repo root carrying exactly `$schema`, `name`, `version`,\n  `description`, `author`, `license`, `keywords`, `repository`. Reuse `description`, `author`,\n  `license`, `keywords` verbatim from the Claude manifest. Omit `displayName` and `skills` \u2014\n  illegal in the closed portable schema. `repository` is\n  `https://git.example.com/ai-tools/dev-workflow`.\n- **Files**: `plugin.json` \u2014 create\n- **Verify**: validates against the 1.0.0 schema; `version` matches step 1.\n\n### Step 3: Record the dual-manifest risk in `CLAUDE.local.md`\n- **Action**: New Gotchas bullet \u2014 the version now lives in two manifests, bumping one alone is\n  silent, and `/workflow-release` bumps neither. Also name both manifests in the \"What this repo\n  is\" opening and correct its stale count (`16 skill` \u2192 `18 skill`, line 7).\n- **Files**: `CLAUDE.local.md` \u2014 modify\n- **Verify**: the bullet names both manifest paths and states that release does not bump them.\n\n### Step 4: Update `README.md`\n- **Action**: (1) new \"Other agents\" subsection under **How it loads** covering conformance, the\n  two-manifest necessity, and why frontmatter stays non-conformant; (2) **Layout** block gains\n  the root `plugin.json`; (3) fix both stale counts (line 3 `17 explicit` \u2192 `18`, line 70\n  `17 skill dirs (14 workflow steps` \u2192 `18 skill dirs (15 workflow steps`); (4) add the missing\n  `/workflow-jira-report` Utilities bullet.\n- **Files**: `README.md` \u2014 modify\n- **Verify**: `ls -d skills/*/ | wc -l` matches the claimed count; `grep -c jira-report README.md` > 0.\n\n### Step 5: Verify the plugin still loads\n- **Action**: Run the schema check and `claude plugin validate . --strict`; confirm `git status\n  --short skills/` is empty.\n- **Files**: none\n- **Verify**: no illegal/missing fields; no *new* validator warnings beyond the pre-existing\n  `CLAUDE.local.md at plugin root` one; no `SKILL.md` modified.\n\n### Risks & Unknowns\n- \u26a0\ufe0f **Version drift between the two manifests** \u2014 accepted deliberately, mitigated only by the\n  step 3 note. `/workflow-release` writes no version file, so nothing enforces it.\n- \u26a0\ufe0f **Frontmatter stays non-conformant** \u2014 all 18 skills fail `skills-ref validate`. Spec \u00a77.1\n  says clients MUST skip such skills; observed clients don't. A bet on observed leniency, not a\n  spec guarantee.\n- \u2753 **`repository` URL unverified** \u2014 derived from the SSH remote, never resolved; may 404.\n- \u2753 **Codex-side loading unproven** \u2014 `codex` not installed here; Cursor never exercised\n  end-to-end.\n- \u2753 **Root `plugin.json` is a new file in Claude Code's plugin root** \u2014 documented as inert,\n  but step 5 is what confirms it.\n\n### Dependencies\n- Step 2 depends on step 1 (version settled before being written twice).\n- Steps 3\u20134 depend on 1\u20132 being final, since they document the result.\n- No external dependencies; no build, test, or lint tooling to satisfy.\n\n## Implementation Status\n\n**Completed**: 2026-08-21\n**Steps completed**: 5 of 5\n**Blocked steps**: none\n\n### Changes Made\n- `.claude-plugin/plugin.json` \u2014 version `1.7.1` \u2192 `1.8.0`; nothing else touched, `displayName`\n  and `skills` deliberately retained (they are recognized Claude Code fields)\n- `plugin.json` \u2014 **new** portable manifest at repo root: `$schema`, `name`, `version`,\n  `description`, `author`, `license`, `keywords`, `repository`. Verified against the published\n  Agent Plugins 1.0.0 schema \u2014 no illegal fields, no missing required fields, `name` matches the\n  spec pattern, `$schema` matches the required const\n- `CLAUDE.local.md` \u2014 opening now names both manifests and the stale count is corrected\n  (`16 skill` \u2192 `18 skill`); two new Gotchas: the version living in two manifests with nothing\n  checking, and the deliberate frontmatter non-conformance with an explicit \"don't fix this to\n  satisfy the validator\"\n- `README.md` \u2014 new \"Other agents\" subsection (conformance, why two manifests, why frontmatter\n  stays non-conformant); Layout block gains the root `plugin.json`; both stale counts corrected\n  (`17 explicit`/`16 workflow-*` \u2192 `18`/`17`, and `17 skill dirs (14 workflow steps` \u2192 `18 skill\n  dirs (15 workflow steps`); new `/workflow-jira-report` Utilities bullet\n\n### Verification Results\n- Portable schema check \u2014 **valid**: no illegal fields, no missing required fields\n- `claude plugin validate . --strict` \u2014 only the pre-existing `CLAUDE.local.md at plugin root`\n  warning, byte-identical to the baseline captured before any edit. **No new warnings.**\n- Both manifests report `\"version\": \"1.8.0\"`\n- `git status --short skills/` \u2014 empty; no `SKILL.md` modified\n- README counts match reality: 18 dirs / 17 `workflow-*`; `jira-report` now documented\n\n### Issues Encountered\n- **One planned unknown resolved.** The plan flagged that a root `plugin.json` sitting in Claude\n  Code's plugin root was untested. `claude plugin validate . --strict` raised no warning about\n  it at all, confirming Claude Code ignores the unrecognized root file as documented. It is\n  inert, not merely tolerated.\n- **`CLAUDE.local.md` never appears in `git diff`** \u2014 it is gitignored by the repo's `*.local*`\n  rule. Its edits are real but will not be part of any commit, so the dual-manifest gotcha lives\n  only on this machine. Worth knowing before relying on it as the team-facing mitigation; the\n  README paragraph is the part that actually ships.\n- Nothing else. The diff touches exactly the four planned files.\n\n## Code Review\n\n**Date**: 2026-08-21\n**Verdict**: \u26a0\ufe0f Approve with comments\n**Criticals**: 0\n**Warnings**: 3\n**Suggestions**: 2\n\nAll 8 acceptance criteria met. Two plan unknowns closed favourably: both the `repository` URL and\nthe `agent-plugins.org` schema URL resolve **200**, so the guessed GitLab URL was correct.\n\n### Findings requiring action\n- [W1] Drift surface is six fields, not one \u2014 `name`, `version`, `description`, `author`,\n  `license`, `keywords` are all duplicated; the gotcha and README name only `version` \u2014\n  `CLAUDE.local.md:40`, `README.md:28`\n- [W2] No repeatable conformance check \u2014 `claude plugin validate .` skips the root manifest, and\n  validating it explicitly uses *Claude Code's* schema, which permits `displayName` where the\n  portable schema forbids it; a regression would pass silently \u2014 `plugin.json`\n- [W3] \"Other agents\" sits under \"How it loads\" but gives no way to load it in a non-Claude\n  client; the `~/.agents/skills` symlink technique already in use is undocumented \u2014 `README.md:19`\n\n### Suggestions\n- [S1] Client list omits ChatGPT (six clients supported at launch) \u2014 `README.md:23`\n- [S2] The `CLAUDE.local.md` gotcha is gitignored and never ships, leaving the README paragraph \u2014\n  the one understating the surface per W1 \u2014 as the only durable mitigation\n\n## Review Fixes\n\n**Date**: 2026-08-21\n**Addressed**: W1, W3, S1, S2 \u2014 W2 declined\n\n- **[W1]** Both places now name all six duplicated fields (`name`, `version`, `description`,\n  `author`, `license`, `keywords`) instead of only `version`. The maintainer-facing detail \u2014\n  which field actually drifts and why, plus the note that `/workflow-release` bumps nothing \u2014\n  stays in `CLAUDE.local.md`; the README keeps just the one-line statement of fact, since\n  validation guidance is not user-facing.\n- **[W2] Declined.** A `scripts/validate-portable-manifest.py` was drafted and rejected: this\n  repo deliberately has no build, test, or lint tooling, and a Python script cuts against that.\n  Instead `CLAUDE.local.md` now states outright that a `claude plugin validate` pass is *not*\n  evidence of portable conformance, and lists the ten fields root `plugin.json` may contain so\n  the check is doable by reading. **The gap is real and remains: nothing mechanical catches a\n  conformance regression.**\n- **[W3]** README now covers pointing the plugin at non-Claude clients. Corrected a wrong\n  assumption raised during review \u2014 a whole-plugin symlink into `~/.agents/skills/` does *not*\n  work, because a skills directory scans for `<name>/SKILL.md` as an immediate child and the\n  plugin root has none (verified: `~/.agents/skills/dev-workflow/SKILL.md` would be missing).\n  Whole-plugin install needs a *plugins* directory (`~/.cursor/plugins/`, `codex plugins\n  install`); a skills directory needs one link per skill, which is why the two pre-existing\n  symlinks on this machine point at individual skills.\n- **[S1]** ChatGPT added to the client list.\n- **[S2]** Addressed by W1 \u2014 the shipped README now carries the complete field list, so the\n  gitignored gotcha is no longer the only place the constraint is recorded.\n\n### Codex verification (2026-08-21, post-review)\n\nAleksandr installed `codex-cli` 0.149.0 and tested it. **Codex sees and uses the plugin's\nskills** via a whole-plugin symlink:\n\n```bash\nln -s ~/.claude/skills/dev-workflow ~/.agents/skills/dev-workflow\n```\n\nThis settles the two largest unknowns carried since planning:\n\n- **Codex-side loading is no longer unproven.** It works.\n- **The frontmatter bet paid off.** All 18 skills carry `model`, `argument-hint`, and\n  `disable-model-invocation` and fail `skills-ref validate`; Agent Plugins \u00a77.1 says a client\n  MUST skip a non-conformant skill. Codex loaded them anyway. The decision to keep\n  `disable-model-invocation` over validator-cleanliness cost nothing in the client it was\n  feared to break.\n\nTwo of my own claims were wrong and are corrected in the README:\n\n- I predicted a whole-plugin symlink into a *skills* directory would fail, because a skills dir\n  scans for `<name>/SKILL.md` as an immediate child and the plugin root has none. Codex handles\n  the plugin-shaped directory regardless. The prediction was wrong; the empirical result stands.\n- I wrote `codex plugins install <path>` into the README. **No such command exists.** Codex has\n  `codex plugin add`, which installs from a *marketplace* (`codex plugin marketplace add`),\n  expecting a `.agents/plugins/marketplace.json` this repo does not ship. The line is removed\n  rather than corrected \u2014 the symlink is the route, and marketplace packaging is out of scope.\n\n### Install documentation (final)\n\nREADME's \"Other agents\" section documents two routes into `~/.agents/skills/`:\n\n- **standalone** \u2014 `git clone ssh://git@git.example.com:2233/ai-tools/dev-workflow.git\n  ~/.agents/skills/dev-workflow`, for users with no Claude Code install at all\n- **symlink** \u2014 `ln -s ~/.claude/skills/dev-workflow ~/.agents/skills/dev-workflow`, one copy\n  serving both clients so a single `git pull` updates them together\n\nThe clone URL was confirmed with `git ls-remote` before being written \u2014 deliberately, after the\ninvented `codex plugins install` reached the README unchecked earlier in this task. Note the\nfull `ssh://` form is required: the remote runs on port **2233**, so the short\n`git@host:path` syntax would silently try port 22 and fail.\n\n### Outstanding\n- \u26a0\ufe0f **W2 stands unmitigated** \u2014 no mechanical check protects Agent Plugins conformance.\n- Cursor remains untested; only Codex was verified. The README no longer claims otherwise.\n\n## Code Review \u2014 2026-08-26 (post-merge re-review)\n\n**Date**: 2026-08-26\n**Scope**: `main...HEAD` after merging `main` (v1.7.3, DW-4) into the branch \u2014 3 files, +52 -6\n**Verdict**: \u274c Request changes\n**Criticals**: 3\n**Warnings**: 2\n**Suggestions**: 2\n\nAll three criticals are the same failure: the six-field identity rule this branch introduced is\nbroken on two of its own fields. Two are original to `d25d4b8`; one arrived with the merge.\n\n### Findings requiring action\n- [C1] `\"license\": \"MIT\"` deleted from the Claude manifest \u2014 `.claude-plugin/plugin.json:9`.\n  Introduced by `d25d4b8` itself (`git log -S'\"license\"'`), not by the merge. Breaks AC 2\n  (byte-identical apart from the version bump) and contradicts the Implementation Status note\n  that nothing else was touched. There is no `LICENSE` file and no README licence statement, so\n  that line was the repo's only MIT declaration.\n- [C2] `license` missing from the portable manifest \u2014 `plugin.json:9`. Plan step 2 lists it among\n  the eight fields; seven shipped. The field is allowed by the portable schema. Combined with C1,\n  `README.md:45` now asserts `license` appears in both manifests when it appears in neither.\n- [C3] `description` drift between manifests \u2014 `plugin.json:5`. Root still reads \"Each step is an\n  explicit `/workflow-*` skill\"; `.claude-plugin/plugin.json` carries the v1.7.3 wording\n  (\"\u2026except branch creation which can also be offered automatically\"). Non-Claude clients would\n  read a description that denies the behaviour v1.7.3 added. This is W1's predicted drift, on the\n  first release after the note was written.\n- [W1] `README.md:13` still claims every step sets `disable-model-invocation: true` \u2014 false since\n  v1.7.3. **Inherited from `main`** (a DW-4 miss), not introduced here, but it sits three lines\n  above the new \"Other agents\" section and this branch is the next release.\n- [W2] The previously declined \"no repeatable conformance check\" has now fired three times.\n  C1\u2013C3 survived implementation, review, review-fixes, and a merge. The reasoning for declining\n  still stands on its merits; the evidence against it is now empirical.\n\n### Suggestions\n- [S1] Both manifests claim `1.8.0` while the newest `CHANGELOG.md` entry is `1.7.3` \u2014 expected\n  mid-flight, but merging without running `/workflow-release` would ship an undocumented version.\n- [S2] Shorten the portable `description`; the clause that drifted describes per-skill invocation\n  mechanics, the part most likely to change again.\n\n### Verified clean\n- `claude plugin validate . --strict` \u2014 identical single pre-existing `CLAUDE.local.md at plugin\n  root` warning; no new warnings\n- 18 skill dirs / 17 `workflow-*`, matching both README counts and the Layout block arithmetic\n- No `SKILL.md` in the diff; `version` identical at `1.8.0` in both manifests; working tree clean\n\n## Review Fixes \u2014 2026-08-26\n\n**Addressed**: C1, C2, C3, W1 \u2014 all four\n\n- **[C1]** `\"license\": \"MIT\"` restored to `.claude-plugin/plugin.json` between `author` and\n  `keywords`, putting the file back to byte-identical-apart-from-the-version-bump and satisfying\n  AC 2. The repo declares MIT again.\n- **[C2]** `\"license\": \"MIT\"` added to root `plugin.json`, completing plan step 2's eight-field\n  list. Root fields are now `$schema`, `name`, `version`, `description`, `author`, `license`,\n  `keywords`, `repository` \u2014 all inside the portable schema's closed allowlist.\n- **[C3]** Root `description` synced to the v1.7.3 wording from `.claude-plugin/plugin.json`.\n  Non-Claude clients no longer read a description that denies `/workflow-branch`'s\n  model-invocability.\n- **[W1]** `README.md:13` rewritten: \"Every step **but one** has `disable-model-invocation: true`\n  \u2026 The exception is `/workflow-branch`, which Claude may offer on its own \u2014 and which always\n  asks before cutting anything.\" Fixes a claim inherited from `main` (a DW-4 miss), so the fix\n  ships from this branch rather than waiting for its own change.\n- **[W2] Still declined, still standing.** Nothing mechanical was added. But the check is now\n  one command, which is what the earlier decline lacked:\n\n      python3 -c \"import json;a=json.load(open('.claude-plugin/plugin.json'));b=json.load(open('plugin.json'));print([f for f in ['name','version','description','author','license','keywords'] if a.get(f)!=b.get(f)] or 'in sync')\"\n\n  Worth adding to `CLAUDE.local.md` alongside the existing `grep -h '\"version\"'` line.\n\n### Verification\n- Six shared fields compared field-by-field \u2014 all identical\n- Root manifest field list checked against the portable allowlist \u2014 conformant\n- `claude plugin validate . --strict` \u2014 unchanged, single pre-existing warning\n\n## Release\n\n**Version**: 1.8.0\n**Date**: 2026-08-26\n**Tag**: v1.8.0\n**Pushed**: no \u2014 `main` is 4 commits ahead of `origin/main`, tag is local only\n\n### Commit\n- `9ffd410` \u2014 chore(DW-2): release v1.8.0 \u2014 add portable agent plugins manifest (tagged v1.8.0)\n\n### Notes\n- Cut on `main`, not on the feature branch. `feature/DW-2_agent-plugins-compatibility` was\n  merged into `main` mid-release (fast-forward, 0/0 divergence at `335cf21`), matching how\n  v1.7.2 and v1.7.3 shipped \u2014 every tag in this repo sits on `main`.\n- Style was chosen at the prompt, not detected: no commitlint config, and 9 of 19 recent\n  subjects were conventional (47%, under the 60% bar).\n- The changelog deliberately omits the C1/C2 license restoration and the C3 description sync.\n  Both defects lived only inside the unreleased DW-2 branch, so no released version was ever\n  affected; the review sections above are their record.\n- Version bump was already in both manifests before release \u2014 `/workflow-release` writes no\n  version file, so `1.7.1` \u2192 `1.8.0` was applied by hand at implementation step 1.\n\n### Outstanding after release\n- Push: `main` + `v1.8.0` tag, plus the merged branch if it should reach the remote.\n- Cursor still untested; only Codex was verified end to end.\n- W2 remains unmitigated in the mechanical sense \u2014 the six-field drift check is now a one-liner\n  in `CLAUDE.local.md`, but nothing runs it automatically.\n"
